{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, PCA, single) scored 0.4849 acc and config_016 (multimodal, PCA+ResNet50, single, concat) scored 0.5266 acc, a ~4-point gain. However, with only two experiments we cannot attribute this gain: it could come from the image modality alone, from genuine cross-modal synergy, or a mix. Uncertainty: We lack the image-only baseline (ResNet50, single profile) to decompose the multimodal result. Question tested: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly measures how much of the 0.5266 is attributable to image features versus RNA features. Why best next step: This single experiment is the highest-information-value test under the limited budget—it tells us whether the fusion is truly additive (image alone << 0.5266) or whether RNA contributes little (image alone ≈ 0.5266). The answer reshapes every subsequent decision: if image dominates, we prioritize image-encoder and aggregation choices; if synergy is real, we invest in fusion strategies and RNA-encoder quality. No other single experiment reduces as much uncertainty about the core design question of this study."
}

